  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nucleophilicity of sulfur-containing nucleophiles (such as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>SH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>) is higher than that of oxygen-containing nucleophiles (such as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>).&nbsp; Here Sulphur containing nucleophile can donate its lone pair. A stable carbocation is formed next, stable carbocation will be that which is away from CN group.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0133_41d295408d4a.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 116px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
